 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-068: Exp4262 Reports Live Completion Metrics Or Blocks Honestly
 **Description:** Running Exp 4262 either writes `blocked_arc_live_env_unreachable` when the SDK import, ARC endpoint, or live scorecard handshake is unavailable, writes `blocked_operator_only_submission` when the only available live path would submit to a leaderboard, or writes a terminal-prefixed live artifact after the scored-only adapter fixture passes, the anonymous-key SDK enumerates the target environment, the margin-triggered solver executes under a bounded completion-sized action budget, and an open scorecard is read without leaderboard submission. A valid reachable artifact MUST set `levels_completed` to the bare integer from the official `EnvironmentScore`, set `actions_vs_baseline_ratio` to the bare float `actions_taken / baseline_actions`, set `leaderboard_submitted=false`, preserve `game_probed`, `actions_taken`, `baseline_actions`, `environment_score`, and `trajectory` evidence, include `preconditions_checked` with SDK reachability plus no-submit verification, declare `random_seed=4262`, compute `reproducibility_checksum` from the probe config and trajectory, include model specs for the live adapter, margin-triggered routing, and provenance-blind routing status, and pass the acceptance gate when those required fields are present with `leaderboard_submitted=false`, including the honest zero-level efficiency-only case.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-069: ARC-AGI-3 Incremental Progress Exp4275 New-Game Offline Advance
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4275 as the next offline ARC-AGI-3 monotonic solved-level attempt after Exp 4261 held the `.394` best at 19 cumulative real-env-confirmed levels on the `sc25-635fd71a` L6 wall. It MUST first confirm that `python/carnot/agentic/arc_agi3_world_model.py` imports and that `results/arc3_win_condition_survey.json` plus local fixture metadata load; otherwise it MUST stop with `honest_verdict="blocked_arc_fixtures_missing"`. It MUST not touch `results/trm_runs/`, MUST not train TRM, and MUST keep the conductor stood down. It MUST select exactly one best-headroom unattempted non-`sc25` game/level from the 25-game survey and local fixture metadata, using the hardened Exp 4244 set-encoder routing artifact as a candidate-ranking readiness gate before committing a route. The offline solver MUST use CPU/cached fixtures, the `GameGraph` explore-induce-verify substrate, hardened set-encoder routing metadata, and real-environment level-counter confirmation before claiming any level increment. The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4275_arc_incremental_progress_new_game.json` MUST include bare top-level fields `honest_verdict`, `total_levels`, `levels_completed`, `game_advanced`, `random_seed`, `reproducibility_checksum`, and `model_specs`, and MUST annotate their principles exactly as follows: `Terminal-prefixed. A +1 advance is success; an honest no-advance (no solvable headroom this game) is COMPLETE and informs the next game pick.`, `BARE int: cumulative solved levels -- target >=20 (monotonic +1 over the .394 19); the north-star accuracy progress metric.`, `BARE int: NEW real-env-confirmed levels this task (>=1 for an advance), from the solver output not a self-report.`, `The game id advanced -- keeps progress attributable per-game; must NOT be sc25 (exp4261's wall).`, `Determinism precondition for the solver run.`, `Hash of the solver inputs + trajectory; lets a third party re-run.`, and `The offline solver + hardened set-encoder routing config; required methodology.`.
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-069: Exp4275 Either Banks One Non-SC25 Level Or Stops Honestly
+**Description:** Running Exp 4275 either writes `blocked_arc_fixtures_missing` when the offline solver import, survey, Exp 4249/4261 prior evidence, Exp 4244 routing artifact, or local fixture metadata cannot support the attempt, writes `complete: incremental_progress_no_advance_<game>_L<n>_<reason>` when the selected non-`sc25` game has no verifier-routed real-env level increment in this bounded run, or writes `success: incremental_progress_<game>_advanced_to_L<n>_total20` only when the offline real environment confirms one new level after the hardened set-encoder route is accepted. A successful run MUST set `total_levels=20`, `levels_completed=1`, `game_advanced` to the non-`sc25` advanced game id, `real_env_confirmed=true`, `verifier_validated=true`, preserve model specs for the offline world-model solver and hardened set-encoder routing, report the selected game/level and why it was selected, and compute `reproducibility_checksum` from deterministic solver inputs and trajectory evidence. An honest no-advance run MUST keep `total_levels=19`, set `levels_completed=0`, set `game_advanced="none"`, set `real_env_confirmed=false`, keep the selected non-`sc25` `target_game` and `target_level` attributable, and still satisfy the acceptance gate when `honest_verdict` is terminal-prefixed with `complete:`. A blocked run MUST keep `total_levels=19`, set `levels_completed=0`, set `game_advanced="none"`, and still satisfy the acceptance gate because the verdict is terminal-prefixed with `blocked_`.
